    ],
    "reading_order": 9,
    "text": "Let us consider the situation again, given in Section 5.1 in which Reena applied for a\njob and got selected. She has been offered the job with a starting monthly salary of\n` 8000, with an annual increment of ` 500. What would be her monthly salary for the\nfifth year?",
    "latex": null,
    "image_ref": null,
    "confidence": 1.0
  },
  {
    "document_id": "NCERT_X_MATH_JEMH105",
    "page": 8,
    "block_id": "jemh105_p008_b10",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "bbox": [
      48.0,
      251.25,
      419.29,
      276.71
    ],
    "reading_order": 10,
    "text": "To answer this, let us first see what her monthly salary for the second year\nwould be.",
    "latex": null,
    "image_ref": null,
    "confidence": 1.0
  },
  {
    "document_id": "NCERT_X_MATH_JEMH105",
    "page": 8,
    "block_id": "jemh105_p008_b11",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "bbox": [
      48.0,
      281.49,
      419.42,
      320.15
    ],
    "reading_order": 11,
    "text": "It would be ` (8000 + 500) = ` 8500. In the same way, we can find the monthly\nsalary for the 3rd, 4th and 5th year by adding ` 500 to the salary of the previous year.\nSo, the salary for the 3rd year = ` (8500 + 500)",
    "latex": null,
    "image_ref": null,
    "confidence": 1.0
  },
  {
    "document_id": "NCERT_X_MATH_JEMH105",
    "page": 8,
    "block_id": "jemh105_p008_b12",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      324.21,
      419.81,
      401.27
    ],
    "reading_order": 12,
    "text": "= ` (8000 + 500 + 500)\n= ` (8000 + 2 × 500)\n= ` [8000 + (3 – 1) × 500]\n(for the 3rd year)\n= ` 9000\nSalary for the 4th year   = ` (9000 + 500)",
    "latex": null,
    "image_ref": null,
    "confidence": 1.0
  },
  {
    "document_id": "NCERT_X_MATH_JEMH105",
    "page": 8,
    "block_id": "jemh105_p008_b13",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "bbox": [
